 (FR-021). Expiry is evaluated at access time — there is no background sweeper (spec
 assumption); an expired record encountered on disk may be removed lazily.
 
+As built, expired records are **not** removed lazily: they stay on disk and are never served.
+No requirement asks for a sweeper, and making a `GET` mutate storage would be a surprise
+(Principle IV). An operator who wants the space back deletes the expired `<id>.json` files,
+which the service tolerates at any time.
+
 **Boundary**: a paste is readable strictly before `expires_at` and gone at or after it —
 `now >= expires_at` means gone (R-009, spec edge case).
 
