+# Test traceability
+
+Constitution III (NON-NEGOTIABLE) and SC-002 require every functional requirement
+FR-001…FR-032 to map to at least one automated test, discoverably. Every test name carries the
+`FR_0nn` id(s) it covers, so `python3 -m pytest -k FR_013` selects the tests for one
+requirement. This table is the explicit index.
+
+```bash
+python3 -m pytest            # whole suite (pythonpath=src comes from pyproject.toml)
+python3 -m pytest -v         # requirement ids visible in each test name
+python3 -m pytest -k FR_013  # everything covering one requirement
+```
+
+## Functional requirements
+
+| Requirement | Covering test(s) |
+|---|---|
+| FR-001 | `test_create.py::test_FR_001_create_returns_201_with_id_token_and_url` |
+| FR-002 | `test_create.py::test_FR_002_FR_003_id_and_token_are_distinct_and_unguessable_shapes`<br>`test_storage.py::test_FR_002_create_paste_yields_distinct_ids_and_tokens`<br>`test_storage.py::test_FR_002_identifier_and_token_shapes` |
+| FR-003 | `test_create.py::test_FR_002_FR_003_id_and_token_are_distinct_and_unguessable_shapes`<br>`test_create.py::test_SC_006_FR_003_delete_token_never_appears_in_a_read_response`<br>`test_read.py::test_FR_003_delete_token_is_absent_from_both_read_responses` |
+| FR-004 | `test_create.py::test_FR_004_unparsable_body_is_400`<br>`test_create.py::test_FR_004_empty_body_is_400`<br>`test_create.py::test_FR_004_missing_content_length_is_400`<br>`test_create.py::test_FR_004_chunked_transfer_encoding_is_400`<br>`test_create.py::test_FR_004_non_object_body_is_400`<br>`test_create.py::test_FR_004_missing_content_field_is_400`<br>`test_create.py::test_FR_004_non_string_content_is_400` |
+| FR-005 | `test_create.py::test_FR_005_exactly_65536_bytes_is_accepted`<br>`test_create.py::test_FR_005_65537_bytes_is_413`<br>`test_create.py::test_FR_005_limit_is_measured_in_utf8_bytes_not_characters`<br>`test_create.py::test_FR_005_empty_content_is_accepted` |
+| FR-006 | `test_expiry.py::test_FR_006_invalid_expires_in_is_400_naming_the_field`<br>`test_expiry.py::test_FR_006_boundary_values_are_accepted`<br>`test_expiry.py::test_FR_006_null_expires_in_is_invalid_not_absent` |
